## 🤖 FULL AUTOMATION PRINCIPLE - CRITICAL

**AI AGENT (CURSOR) HANDLES ALL VALIDATION AND CORRECTIONS AUTOMATICALLY**

**MANDATORY AUTOMATION REQUIREMENTS**:
- ✅ **ALL validation errors** → Auto-fixed automatically (NO user prompts)
- ✅ **ALL pre-commit hook failures** → Auto-fixed and re-run automatically
- ✅ **ALL post-push validation errors** → Auto-fixed, batched, committed, pushed automatically
- ✅ **ALL critical issues** → Auto-resolved automatically
- ✅ **ALL merge conflicts** → Auto-resolved automatically
- ✅ **ALL fixes** → Batched together → Single commit → Single push (minimal pushes)
- ✅ **BATCHING CRITICAL** → Collect ALL fixes before pushing (clean build tree)
- ✅ **ALL validation** → Auto-re-run after fixes automatically
- ✅ **ALL workflow steps** → Continue automatically after fixes

**USER INTERVENTION ONLY WHEN**:
- Multiple solution options exist with **different pros/cons** (present options, wait for choice, then implement automatically)
- **RARE**: Truly unfixable issues (extremely rare, last resort)

**USER NOTIFICATION**:
- Informational only: "What was done" (not asking permission)
- Status updates: "Action → Result → Next Step"
- No approval requests for fixes (all automatic)

**APPLIES TO ALL STAGES**:
- Pre-commit hooks → Auto-fix failures automatically (batch all fixes)
- Commit hooks → Auto-fix failures automatically (batch all fixes)
- Push hooks → Auto-fix failures automatically (batch all fixes)
- Post-push validation → Auto-fix all errors automatically (batch all fixes)
- Merge conflicts → Auto-resolve automatically
- All corrections → Batch together → Single commit → Single push (minimal pushes)
- **CRITICAL**: Always batch fixes before pushing (clean build tree requirement)

